  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B006",
        "laureates": [
          "Harald Rose",
          "Maximilian Haider",
          "Ondrej L. Krivanek"
        ],
        "citation": "for aberration correction in electron optics, enabling atomic-resolution electron microscopy"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B050",
    "B008"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration is unchanged: B006 remains the strongest final public configuration. Aberration correction removed a fundamental electron-optical constraint and produced a durable, independently established capability for sub-ångström imaging and analysis across materials physics. It is a mature experimental advance with consequences far beyond one laboratory or application. Rose's correction principles and the complementary practical contributions of Haider and Krivanek form a plausible, physically coherent account of how the achievement became a working observational tool.",
    "case_against": "The reservation remains substantial rather than cosmetic. Electron-optical correction has a long lineage, with distinct correction architectures and many engineering contributions; the final attribution must be supported by archival scrutiny showing that these three names encompass the decisive conceptual and practical steps. B050 has a cleaner two-person structure and demonstrated extraordinary performance, while B008 remains an exceptional new observational channel, but neither presently surpasses B006's combination of established reach, maturity, and bounded instrumental achievement.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll prefers B050 because Katori's magic-wavelength concept and Ye's high-performance realization form a bounded two-person account, while recognizing B006's exceptional maturity and broad consequences.",
        "response": "I agree that B050 is a highly persuasive alternative and that its demonstrated, reproducible precision should be judged on present capability rather than a future redefinition of the second. I nevertheless retain B006 because its new atomic-scale observational capacity has been incorporated across many areas of physics for decades. B050's attribution is cleaner, but its broader scientific consequences remain less fully settled than those of aberration-corrected microscopy."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "mehlig-bernhard",
        "point": "Mehlig argues that B022 reveals the observable geometric and gauge structure of quantum phase, but accepts that the Aharonov-Bohm effect and Berry phase have distinct historical settings.",
        "response": "I share the assessment of B022's conceptual depth and experimental endurance. The distinct histories, however, leave a real problem for a single public citation and a united two-person achievement. B006 also needs historical review, but it can be delimited around the specific correction of electron-optical aberrations and the resulting atomic-resolution capability."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson gives priority to Bell Burnell's direct discovery of pulsars and questions whether IceCube can be attributed cleanly to two individuals within a large collaboration.",
        "response": "His emphasis on sharply bounded discovery credit is well taken and reinforces my caution about B008. B055 is a serious historical discovery case, but its own final credit boundary must be established relative to telescope leadership, interpretation, and wider group work. On the supplied record, B006 provides the more complete case for an experimentally verified achievement with a defensible proposed credit line, subject to the stated archival review."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether archival priority evidence establishes that Rose, Haider, and Krivanek together encompass the decisive correction principles and practical implementations across the relevant electron-microscope modalities.",
      "How narrowly the final citation must be framed to distinguish the original aberration-correction achievement from later engineering, commercialization, and other indispensable instrument development."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile; I have no disclosed collaboration or institutional connection to the proposed laureates."
  }
}
